N3TR-E thumbnail 3†assets.lcsc.com L1217:   * Pinout\\nL1218: \\nL1219:   * Footprint\\nL1220: \\nL1221: Images for reference only\\nL1222: # ST VNL5050N3TR-E\\nL1223: \\nL1224: Manufacturer  | cite561†ST L1225: MPN  | VNL5050N3TR-E\\nL1226: LCSC Part #  | C2680415\\nL1227: Packaging  | SOT-223\\nL1228: Customer #  | [Input: Customer Number]\\nL1229: Key Attributes  | fully protected low-side driver\\nL1230: Datasheet  | cite562†ST VNL5050N3TR-E L1231: RoHS Compliance  | 3 documents available\\nL1232: ## Products Specifications\\nL1233: \\nL1234: All[Input]\\nL1235: Type  | Description  |\\nL1236: --- | --- | ---\\nL1237: Category  | cite415†Integrated Circuits (ICs)/Power Management (PMIC)/Power Distribution Switches, Load Drivers | [Input]\\nL1238: Manufacturer  | cite561†ST | [Input]\\nL1239: Packaging  | SOT-223  | [Input]\\nL1240: Operating Temperature  | -40℃~+150℃  | [Input]\\nL1241: Features  | Overcurrent Protection;Short-Circuit Protection;Over temperature protection;Overvoltage protection  | [Input]\\nL1242: number of channels  | 1  | [Input]\\nL1243: Control Input Logic  | Active High  | [Input]\\nL1244: Maximum Continuous Current  | 19A  | [Input]\\nL1245: RDS(on)  | 50mΩ  | [Input]\\nL1246: Operating Voltage  | 3.5V~5.5V  | [Input]\\nL1247: Type  | Low Side Switch  | [Input]\\nL1248: Type  | Description  |\\nL1249: --- | --- | ---\\nL1250: Category  | cite415†Integrated Circuits (ICs)/Power Management (PMIC)/Power Distribution Switches, Load Drivers | [Input]\\nL1251: Manufacturer  | cite561†ST | [Input]\\nL1252: Packaging  | SOT-223  | [Input]\\nL1253: Operating Temperature  | -40℃~+150℃  | [Input]\\nL1254: Features  | Overcurrent Protection;Short-Circuit Protection;Over temperature protection;Overvoltage protection  | [Input]\\nL1255: number of channels  | 1  | [Input]\\nL1256: Type  | Description  |\\nL1257: --- | --- | ---\\nL1258: Control Input Logic  | Active High  | [Input]\\nL1259: Maximum Continuous Current  | 19A  | [Input]\\nL1260: RDS(on)  | 50mΩ  | [Input]\\nL1261: Operating Voltage  | 3.5V~5.5V  | [Input]\\nL1262: Type  | Low Side Switch  | [Input]\\nL1263: \\nL1264: Help & Feedbackcite415†Show similar products (0) > L1265: ## Introduction\\nL1266: \\nL1267: AI Translation\\nL1268: The VNL5050N3-E and VNL5050S5-E are monolithic devices made using VIPower Technology, intended for driving resistive or inductive loads with one side connected to the battery. Built-in thermal shutdown protects the chip from overtemperature and short-circuit. Output current limitation protects the devices in an overload condition. In case of long duration overload, the devices limit the dissipated power to a safe level up to thermal shutdown intervention.\\nL1269: Thermal shutdown, with automatic restart, allows the devices to recover normal operation as soon as a fault condition disappears. Fast demagnetization of inductive loads is achieved at turn-off.\\nL1270: ## Features\\nL1271: \\nL1272: AI Translation\\nL1273: \\nL1274:   * Automotive qualified\\nL1275:   * Drain current: 19 A\\nL1276:   * ESD protection\\nL1277:   * Overvoltage clamp\\nL1278:   * Thermal shutdown\\nL1279:   * Current and power limitation\\nL1280:   * Very low standby current\\nL1281:   * Very low electromagnetic susceptibility\\nL1282:   * Compliant with European directive 2002/95/EC\\nL1283:   * Open drain status output (VNL5050S5-E only)\\nL1284: \\nL1285: Every Order Guarantee\\nL1286: \\nL1287: 100% Authentic · 30-Day Return or Replacement\\nL1288: \\nL1289: Out of Stock\\nL1290: \\nL1291: Notify Me\\nL1292: \\nL1293: Minimum: 1 Multiple: 1 Sales Unit: Piece\\nL1294: \\nL1295: [Input]\\nL1296: \\nL1297: Add to Cart\\n\"\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"TJA1051\",\n    \"url\": \"https://cache.nxp.com/docs/en/data-sheet/TJA1051.pdf\",\n    \"bytes\": 209490,\n    \"sha256\": \"6637cd500dda3c1c951ce29bed7fe909f11f9a3bef64b096dbb486827add9f11\",\n    \"pdftotext_returncode\": 0,\n    \"stderr\": \"\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"VNL5090\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/vnl5090n3-e.pdf\",\n    \"error\": \"The read operation timed out\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"MAX9924\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX9924-MAX9927.pdf\",\n    \"error\": \"The read operation timed out\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"MAX9142\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX9140-MAX9144.pdf\",\n    \"error\": \"The read operation timed out\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"TLE9201\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-TLE9201SG-DS-v01_05-en.pdf?fileId=db3a30431b3e89eb011ba415a2e24797\",\n    \"error\": \"HTTP Error 404: Not Found\"\n  }\n]# Physical review experiments\n\nCandidate: 69119fab9d25319b3bf376eca634b13104ba76b7417416b85a2a64a4e78a6ab4\nRun: f3c237c2-3a08-4617-aaba-f04c47bbe98f\nPacket SHA256: c2f38615ec9fb1bb4b8e95f9e23e73f328ff00f06c4539ca8b66926e0890d4e7\nRole: physical\n\n## Commands, tools, and preservation\n\n`python3 /work/experiments/run_checks.py` recorded exact subprocess argv, exit codes, UTC start times and output-log paths in commands.json. Tools: KiCad CLI 10.0.7; Python 3.12.3. Its native DRC rerun and separate plated/unplated Excellon and Gerber exports read /candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb directly. No --check-zones option, zone refill, board save, or scratch board mutation was used. The exports are diagnostic experiments, not manufacturing release files.\n\n`/usr/bin/python3 /work/experiments/measure_board.py > /work/experiments/measure-board.log 2>&1` reads the saved board using pcbnew 10.0.7, measures nominal holes, compares numbered pad nets with the full native XML netlist, inventories CAN2 population and selected power/return copper, and plots three thermal regions. See board-measurements.json and thermal-reliefs.png. The plot uses exact native saved zone/pad polygons but approximate rendered track stroke widths; it is illustrative and does not replace native DRC or a geometric tolerance calculation.\n\n`/usr/bin/python3 /work/experiments/audit_records.py > /work/experiments/audit-records.log 2>&1` records source/evidence hashes, compares DRC categories/exclusions, and queries direct ground track connections at the flagged thermal pads. See input-hashes.json, drc-comparison.json, thermal-track-connections.json. Board SHA256 remained 4e059d571e0f46911d9101b86c8178298cefb866e2f19d5295a30c35dadedd53. Upper/lower-case VR sheet copies have identical SHA256 377a2691ec878301977100851c40e302b2b7864d88cc27c6c305c03bbf14e15b.\n\nAdditional read-only probes: rg --files for project/check inventory; Python json inspection of complete /evidence/work/drc/drc.json, /evidence/work/erc/erc.json, connectivity.json, and native .kicad_pro settings; sed/rg for native PCB pad UUIDs and zone definitions. `kicad-cli pcb export gerbers --help` and `kicad-cli pcb export drill --help` confirmed the explicit refill option and separate TH drill option. A preliminary pcbnew probe tried unavailable FOOTPRINT.GetProperties and raised AttributeError; the corrected probes use supported methods. pcbnew also emits three PROPERTY_ENUM 'No enum choices defined' diagnostics on import/load in this environment; subsequent reads and measurements completed. These tool diagnostics are not native electrical violations.\n\n## Outcomes and adjudication\n\n1. Supplied native DRC: 142 violations, 0 unconnected items, 114 schematic parity warnings. All 13 error-severity entries explicitly carry excluded=true and blank comments. They are three starved_thermal entries and five mechanical padstack entries plus five annular_width entries describing the same five holes. No count is treated as a behavioral test.\n2. Independent DRC: 156 violations, 0 unconnected items, 114 parity warnings. The 13 error entries reproduce. Library coverage differs: this local rerun reports 129 missing-library entries, whereas the supplied check environment resolves stock libraries and reports 106 library footprint mismatches plus 9 missing-library entries. This difference is an environment limitation, not a newly discovered physical defect. See drc-comparison.json.\n3. All 694 numbered PCB pad instances compared with native XML have identical net names. The remaining 25 pads are anonymous mechanical or paste geometry. This confirms nominal pad assignments, not fabricated continuity, component internals, or correct circuit behavior. Source hierarchy includes ten instances and byte-identical disposable VR sheet alias.\n4. Five anonymous J1 holes at (71.95,35.49), (75.55,39.34), (120.00,28.49), (199.65,39.34), (203.25,35.49) mm are native PTH. Three have pad/drill diameter 4.0/4.0 mm; two have 2.2/2.2 mm. Circular nominal annulus=(pad diameter-drill diameter)/2=0.0 mm. Native DRC cites a 0.1 mm configured minimum, with explicit exclusions. Separate drill export puts all five in Polygonus-Universal-Base-PTH.drl (T10 and T12); NPTH file is empty. This supports a manufacturing concern about the plated/zero-ring representation. It does not establish a signal connection failure: these are no-net mounting holes, and connector/fabricator intent and finished-hole tolerances are not established.\n5. Starved relief entries: C15.2, U7.4, C14.2 have one native F.Cu zone relief spoke versus configured minimum two; all three are excluded. Each also has explicit ground trace connections (0.25 mm) toward nearby ground vias. See exact track UUIDs in thermal-track-connections.json and thermal-reliefs.png. Therefore the zone-spoke warning alone does not demonstrate a floating ground, inadequate return, or thermal failure, and is not raised as an electrical defect.\n6. CAN2: native PCB and schematic connect J1.15/J2.73/U20.7/U21.7/R36.1/R37.1 to CAN2+, and corresponding J1.11/J2.74/U20.6/U21.6/R36.2/R37.2 to CAN2-. R36 and R37 are both 120 ohm DNP. Native netlist retains DNP pin connectivity; it must not be mistaken for populated termination. Selected bus track total lengths are approximately 252.43/252.40 mm, including all branches; these totals are not endpoint path lengths or impedance measurements. No donor-only model establishes module/harness termination, populated end-to-end resistance, transceiver signal integrity, or dynamic operation. Absence of populated carrier termination is not sufficient to assert failure with unspecified module/harness circuitry.\n7. Saved stackup declares four copper layers and 0.035 mm nominal copper per layer. Selected 12 V, ground and heater paths were inventoried in board-measurements.json. Width and via counts were not converted to ampacity or thermal qualification: operating currents, simultaneity, copper tolerances, ambient, enclosure cooling and allowed rise were not established. No load stimulus was invented.\n8. Full ERC was read for coverage and error categories. Power-drive annotation and duplicate power-output types do not independently prove absent supply or contention inside modular circuitry. The 353-entry ERC report is not an operating circuit test; not every warning received component-specific adjudication in this physical review.\n\n## Coverage omissions and limitations\n\nNo candidate changes, refill comparison, manufactured-board continuity/ohmmeter tests, powered measurements, SPICE simulation, CAN waveforms/bit-rate sweeps, or electrical behavioral proof. No complete module-internal or harness termination review; no inferred module ratings/models. No connector drawing/finished-hole fit verification, fabricator capability/tolerance review, 3D assembly/case/height clearance qualification, or comprehensive independent pad-land-pattern validation. Selected local placement/ground-relief inspection is not a full mechanical assembly audit. No DC load/current-sharing, fault protection coordination, ampacity, temperature-rise, junction-temperature or cooling qualification. No automotive transient, ignition energy, wideband stability, EMC, or integrated FOME-MC qualification. Saved copper only; zero native unconnected items does not prove correct physical behavior. No external references fetched; findings rely on native geometry and generated local fabrication outputs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
